 {chapter:'ENDING',tag:'THE WEDDING PHOTO',caption:'“Kimi’s speech is only twelve minutes long.”',art:'festival',speaker:'NARRATOR',ending:'married',text:'You and Emi start dating, one honest conversation at a time. Years later, you marry beneath a canopy of festival lanterns. Your vows are sweet, sincere, and mercifully free of sibling-made slides.\n\nKimi gives a toast. She cries, laughs, and only mentions the beach towel incident twice. As your little sister, she gets the first dance after the newlyweds. The family photo includes one tiny houseplant in a party hat.\n\n<strong>ROMANCE ENDING · HAPPILY EVER AFTER</strong>'},
